WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh!
-Was this a baby shower?

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.369 size:75% position:38%
-It's a baby shower.
-So Serena Williams.

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You were at her baby shower.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You're good friends

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.106
with Serena, and it was --
it looks like, what is it,

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
'50s sock hop theme?
-'50S. It's a '50s theme.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:12.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
Serena's really big on
theme parties, which is, like,

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
such a pain in the ass.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I'm so happy

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
to hear you say that.
-[ Sighs ]

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because friends who are
into theme parties,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's such a burden.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's such a burden.
I gotta go find an outfit.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to make sure it fits.
Like, actually,

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you look closely at
my dress,

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went to a Halloween shop
in Miami Beach

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.627 line:92%
'cause this was in Florida.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.496 line:92%
And there's pirates on my dress,

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it's actually
a pirate outfit,

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I couldn't find
a '50s outfit.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.902
-Oh, my goodness.
-But I sewed it to make it look

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a '50s outfit.
-That's very impressive.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.839
Now is she the kind of person
who has a theme party and if you

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:43.209
had shown up in sort of --
-Oh, you get like, shade.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.112
You get the looks of like,
"oh, you didn't dress up."

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Too good for the '50s.
-Too good to dress up, huh?

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, so you have to.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.653
-You mention that you sewed it.
You actually know how to sew.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which -- I want to talk about
your fashion line.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.623
-Yeah.
-but I feel like a lot of people

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
have fashion lines,
and I feel like there are many

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have never sewn.
-Right.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you are --
-No, I sew.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:04.330
I mean, I don't sew each piece
in my fashion line. [ Laughs ]

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:04.998 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Right. Yeah.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.800 size:78% position:39%
-But I've been sewing
since I was, like, 7.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to sew, like, curtains
and pillows and then I --

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.605
-When you sewed curtains,
were they for your room

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
or for other people? Okay.
-Yeah. Both, both.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
I actually started because,
I had an aunt who always said,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Make your house a home,"
and so when she'd come over,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.880
she'd get really mad if we
didn't have curtains, or...

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"I can't afford curtains."

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would go
to the fabric place

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
and buy the discount fabric
and then make curtains.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.422
-That's great. Could you tell it
was discount fabric?

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like, did the sun come

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
right through it?
-Yeah.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Actually, it caught on fire

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
a couple of times.
-Yeah, right. [ Laughs ]

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Highly flammable material.
-[ Laughs ] Right.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-And then, over the years,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.866 size:81% position:41%
have you done other --
have you sewn other --

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.735
-Oh, yeah, no. Then I evolved to
Halloween costumes

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
for my nieces and nephews
and then to dresses.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would, like, make dresses
for my girlfriends.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now -- now I'm just
a seamstress to my friends.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, they bring pants
over and like,

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
"can you hem these?"
-Really?

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:54.247
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-I would think they would assume

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have more important things
to do than hem their pants.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, apparently not.
-Wow.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I'd like to sew --

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd like to learn how to sew
a Halloween costume.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh! Oh, they're hard.
-I think I would feel -- yeah.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.190 size:84% position:42%
They're actually hard.
-Don't start with them?

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
Start with flammable curtains?
Yeah.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:06.893
-Yeah.
Start with straight lines, yeah.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-One time, my nephew --

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always let my nieces
and nephews pick

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
what they want to be, and then
I go find the pattern.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:15.468
And so one's, like, a vampire.
I'm like, good, great, easy.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know? Princess, got it,
That's a dress.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then one year

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
my nephew goes, "spider!"
and I was like, ooh.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:23.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Ooh.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a lot of legs and --
-Exactly.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.779
-Ah, that's a lot of work.
How about -- How about --

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.382
Why don't we use vampire again?
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.684
You're going to be half
a spider, with four legs.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-And two of them are

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:35.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
going to be your arms. Um...
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.924
-So, this is your fashion line,
and this is a photo shoot.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:38.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-These are the ads

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
for your fashion line,
and these are --

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Those are my dogs!
-Actual dogs that you used.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I will say --

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jinxy and Popeye,
which is "Popeye" in Spanish.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.334 line:92%
-And they look very dignified,

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.738
and they look like they are
professional dog models.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:54.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, they are assholes.
-They were?

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:54.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.776
-Was it a bad scene? 'Cause I've
take an few photos

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
with my dog,
and it's a bad scene.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, they're not cooperative
at all.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.549
This was the one frame that they
were actually cooperating.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-If you saw all

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
